.TH "MITSUBISHI\-ECHONET" "1" "November 2026" "mitsubishi\-echonet 0.1.0" "Mitsubishi ECHONET Manual"
.SH NAME
mitsubishi\-echonet \- local ECHONET Lite control for Mitsubishi Wi-Fi adapters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mitsubishi\-echonet [\-\-version] COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Enable, disable and verify local ECHONET Lite control on Mitsubishi Electric MAC\-577IF\-E\-class Wi\-Fi adapters. Run only on a trusted network: ECHONET Lite has no authentication.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable
enable ECHONET Lite via the /smart endpoint
.TP
.B disable
disable ECHONET Lite via the /smart endpoint
.TP
.B status
read\-only check: is the adapter reachable and is ECHONET Lite on?
.TP
.B capabilities
read\-only: list the adapter's supported ECHONET properties (incl. timers)
.TP
.B discover
multicast discovery of ECHONET Lite devices
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed (adapter unreachable, command rejected, or no device found).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (invalid or missing arguments).
